---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import EditorialSources from "../../components/EditorialSources.astro";
import { editorialSources } from "../../data/editorialSources";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Why Sync Licensing Matters | How Much Music"
  description="How film, TV, ads, trailers, games, and social reuse can reshape a song's long-term catalog earnings."
  type="article"
>
  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">Explainer</p>
    <h1>Why sync licensing matters</h1>
    <p class="page-updated">Updated July 29, 2026</p>
    <p>
      A sync placement can create direct licensing income and renewed listener attention. The size
      of a particular fee is usually private, so it should not be inferred from the visibility of a placement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why some songs sync well</h2>
    <ul class="meta-list">
      <li>Immediate emotional clarity.</li>
      <li>Strong cultural recognition.</li>
      <li>Flexible use in film, TV, trailers, games, or short-form video.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How sync can affect the model</h2>
    <ul class="meta-list">
      <li>A placement can create a direct licensing fee, but those fees are rarely public at song-page level.</li>
      <li>A placement can also create secondary demand by sending listeners back to streaming platforms.</li>
      <li>Recognizable catalog songs can become more valuable because they reduce creative risk for supervisors and advertisers.</li>
      <li>Sync is treated as context for range confidence, not as a precise disclosed line item unless public evidence exists.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why it changes long-term earnings</h2>
    <p>
      Sync use can push an older recording back into playlists, charts, social media edits, and
      catalog discovery. That public attention can be discussed separately from any private fee.
    </p>
    <p>
      The important distinction is direct versus indirect value. Direct value is the placement
      itself; indirect value is the long-tail discovery that can follow when a song becomes useful
      again in a new cultural context.
    </p>
  </section>

  <EditorialSources sources={editorialSources.sync} title="Licensing and rights background" />
</BaseLayout>
